#!/usr/bin/env python3
r"""Own, validate, query, and plan CSW ``task.yml`` controls.

This executable requires Python 3.10+ and PyYAML (``python -m pip install
PyYAML``; development uses PyYAML 6.0.3).  It is both a CLI and an importable
public API despite having no ``.py`` suffix::

    api = runpy.run_path(".omp/csw/bin/task_ctl")
    api["get_task"](Path.cwd(), ".cswd/tasks/example")

The public API is ``TaskCtlError``, ``task_dir(repo, task_id)``,
``get_task(repo, task_id)``, ``set_task(repo, task_id, updates,
replace=False)``, ``list_tasks(repo, task_id, impl=False)``,
``parse_config(text)``, ``detect_cycle(edges)``, and ``scan_tasks(repo,
task_id)``. ``scan_tasks`` returns the same direct-child records as ``list_tasks``
but represents a malformed child's control as ``{task-id: ..., error: ...}``,
so execution can retain that blocker while continuing independent tasks.
Container/path errors still raise. ``plan_tasks`` is also available for callers
that want the CLI's mechanical planning operation.

Schema
------
A control is a YAML mapping containing only these keys, in this form::

    type: impl                    # impl or hld
    status: ready                 # new, critic, planned, ready, verified, done
    order: 2                      # optional nonnegative integer; bool is invalid
    priority: P1                  # optional P0, P1, P2, or P3
    blocked-by:                   # optional; unique exact task IDs
      - task-id: .cswd/tasks/parent/01-contract
        remarks: API must exist   # optional string
    source: .cswd/tasks/parent/spec.md  # optional safe repo-relative spec.md

``impl`` identifies a direct executable leaf.  ``hld`` identifies a design or
container that must be decomposed before implementation.  Priority ordering is
P0 (highest) through P3 (lowest); it is a stable scheduling tie-breaker, not a
dependency.

``new`` is newly recorded, ``critic`` means its specification critique is
complete, ``planned`` means its required decomposition is complete, ``ready``
means an implementation result is awaiting parent verification, ``verified``
means verification passed but integration is pending, and ``done`` is
integrated completion.  Only ``done`` in the repository tree being queried
satisfies a dependency.  ``running``, ``blocked``, and ``failed`` are execution
outcomes, not lifecycle statuses; they belong in ``task.md`` evidence (under
``**Outcome:**``), never in ``task.yml``.

New controls default only ``type: hld`` and ``status: new``.  Optional fields
stay absent until supplied.  A whole replacement of an existing control must
explicitly include both required fields; replacement creates with defaults
only when no control exists.  A merge update preserves omitted stored fields.
Unknown or duplicate YAML keys, YAML values with the wrong shape or type,
duplicate blockers, and unsafe paths are errors.

IDs and paths
-------------
Exact canonical task IDs are POSIX repository-relative directory paths below
``.cswd/tasks`` or ``docs/changes``, for example
``docs/changes/parser/03-errors``.  API calls and ``blocked-by.task-id`` always
require that exact form.  CLI task arguments additionally accept ``parser``
as shorthand for ``.cswd/tasks/parser``; there is no basename search or
``docs/changes`` shorthand.  ``.cswd/tasks`` and ``docs/changes`` themselves
are accepted only as ``list`` containers.  Absolute paths, backslashes,
empty/``.``/``..`` components, surrounding whitespace, and paths whose
symlinks escape the repository are rejected.  ``source`` follows the same
safe repo-relative rules and its final component must be ``spec.md``.

Commands
--------
All commands accept global ``--repo PATH`` before the command; it defaults to
the current directory and may name an explicit worktree.

``get TASK [SELECTOR]`` reads one control.  At most one of ``--all``,
``--type``, ``--status``, ``--order``, ``--priority``, ``--blocked``,
``--source``, and ``--spec`` may be supplied.  No selector and ``--all`` both
emit the stored mapping as block YAML.  Scalar selectors emit their plain
scalar value; a missing optional scalar emits an empty line.  ``--blocked``
always emits YAML and defaults to ``[]`` when absent.  ``--spec`` prints the
absolute task-local sibling ``spec.md`` path without reading Markdown or
requiring either ``task.yml`` or ``spec.md`` to exist.

``set TASK [field options]`` merges ``--type``, ``--status``, ``--order``,
``--priority``, ``--source``, and repeatable ``--blocked YAML`` updates.
Each ``--blocked`` value may be one blocker mapping or a list of mappings;
``--blocked '[]'`` clears the list.  ``set TASK YAML`` and
``set TASK --all YAML`` are equivalent whole replacements.  Whole YAML,
``--all``, and field options are mutually exclusive, and repeated scalar
field options are rejected before mutation.  With no options, ``set TASK``
creates a default control when absent or performs a validated no-op merge when
present.  The resulting complete mapping is emitted as YAML.  If TASK is
absent, only its immediate directory is created and only when its parent
already exists; parent trees are never invented.  A directory that exists
without a control is a new control.

Shell quoting examples::

    task_ctl --repo "$PWD" get docs/changes/parser/03-errors --status
    task_ctl set parser --status planned --priority P1
    task_ctl set parser/leaf --blocked \
      '{task-id: .cswd/tasks/parser/01-contract, remarks: needs API}'
    task_ctl set parser/leaf --blocked \
      '[{task-id: .cswd/tasks/parser/01-contract}]'
    task_ctl set parser/leaf --all $'type: impl\nstatus: ready\nblocked-by: []'
    task_ctl set parser/leaf $'type: impl\nstatus: ready'

Use flow-style YAML for option arguments that might otherwise begin with a
hyphen.  For a positional block sequence, terminate option parsing explicitly,
for example ``task_ctl plan parser -- $'- slug: api\n  type: impl\n  priority: P0'``.

``list TASK [--impl] [--full]`` examines the TASK directory's direct-child
controls.  It does not require a control on TASK itself, so both canonical
roots are useful containers.  An immediate child is a task candidate only
when it contains ``spec.md`` or ``task.yml``.  A candidate with a
specification but no control fails closed; unrelated directories and empty
collision reservations are ignored.  Results are ordered by numeric
``order`` then canonical ID, with missing orders last.  The default output is
raw canonical IDs, one per line (and no output for an empty result).
``--full`` instead emits a YAML list of records shaped
``{task-id: CANONICAL_ID, ...full stored config...}``.  ``--impl`` filters
either representation to unfinished (``status != done``) ``impl`` leaves,
excludes a direct child that is itself a container of controlled descendants,
and keeps a leaf only when every exact dependency exists and is ``done``.
Missing dependencies wait rather than satisfy.  Existing dependency cycles
among unfinished tasks are errors; completed tasks are satisfied terminals.

``plan PARENT YAML`` is read-only mechanical planning.  PARENT must have a
safe existing task-local ``spec.md``.  YAML is a list in requirement order;
each candidate has exactly ``slug``, ``type``, ``priority``, and optional
``blocked-by``.  Slugs are unique lowercase kebab-case.  A blocker task-id is
either another candidate slug or an exact canonical external ID.  The command
rejects cycles, performs a stable topological sort (ready candidates by P0
through P3, then input order), assigns contiguous orders from 1 and at-least
two-digit ``NN-slug`` child IDs, converts candidate blockers to those final
IDs, sets ``status: new`` and ``source: PARENT/spec.md``, and emits the proposed
records with a ``collision`` boolean.  It never creates or changes files;
the caller resolves semantic equivalence and collisions and reruns.

Controls are authoritative.  Commands never inspect lifecycle metadata in
Markdown and never fall back when ``task.yml`` is missing.  ``task.md`` is
implementation evidence only; current execution outcomes may be recorded
there under ``**Outcome:**`` by the execution workflow.

Writes use a temporary file plus ``os.replace`` so each control-file change is
atomic, and all CLI, schema, and path validation happens before mutation.
Creating a new task directory and its control cannot be one filesystem
transaction; a late operating-system failure may leave an empty newly created
directory, which the command attempts to remove.

Exit status 0 means success.  Status 2 means command usage, validation, path,
dependency, or handled filesystem failure; the diagnostic is on stderr and no
traceback is printed.  Unexpected interpreter failures retain Python's nonzero
exit behavior.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
from collections.abc import Iterable, Mapping
import os
from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath
import re
import sys
import tempfile
from typing import Any

import yaml


ROOTS = (".cswd/tasks", "docs/changes")
CONFIG_KEYS = ("type", "status", "order", "priority", "blocked-by", "source")
CONFIG_KEY_SET = frozenset(CONFIG_KEYS)
TYPES = frozenset(("impl", "hld"))
STATUSES = frozenset(("new", "critic", "planned", "ready", "verified", "done"))
PRIORITIES = frozenset(("P0", "P1", "P2", "P3"))
SLUG_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$")


class TaskCtlError(RuntimeError):
    """A user-actionable task control, graph, or path error."""


class _UniqueKeyLoader(yaml.SafeLoader):
    pass


def _construct_unique_mapping(loader: yaml.SafeLoader, node: yaml.nodes.MappingNode, deep: bool = False) -> dict[Any, Any]:
    loader.flatten_mapping(node)
    result: dict[Any, Any] = {}
    for key_node, value_node in node.value:
        key = loader.construct_object(key_node, deep=deep)
        try:
            duplicate = key in result
        except TypeError as exc:
            raise yaml.constructor.ConstructorError(
                "while constructing a mapping",
                node.start_mark,
                "found an unhashable mapping key",
                key_node.start_mark,
            ) from exc
        if duplicate:
            raise yaml.constructor.ConstructorError(
                "while constructing a mapping",
                node.start_mark,
                f"found duplicate key {key!r}",
                key_node.start_mark,
            )
        result[key] = loader.construct_object(value_node, deep=deep)
    return result


_UniqueKeyLoader.add_constructor(
    yaml.resolver.BaseResolver.DEFAULT_MAPPING_TAG,
    _construct_unique_mapping,
)


def _load_yaml(text: str, label: str) -> Any:
    if not isinstance(text, str):
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{label} must be YAML text")
    try:
        return yaml.load(text, Loader=_UniqueKeyLoader)
    except yaml.YAMLError as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"invalid {label}: {exc}") from exc


def _normalize_repo(repo: Path) -> Path:
    try:
        resolved = Path(repo).resolve()
    except (OSError, RuntimeError) as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"cannot resolve repository path {repo}: {exc}") from exc
    if not resolved.is_dir():
        raise TaskCtlError(f"repository directory not found: {resolved}")
    return resolved


def _is_relative_to(path: Path, parent: Path) -> bool:
    try:
        path.relative_to(parent)
        return True
    except ValueError:
        return False


def _safe_relative(value: str, label: str) -> PurePosixPath:
    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{label} must be a nonempty string")
    if value != value.strip():
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{label} must not contain surrounding whitespace: {value!r}")
    if value.startswith("/") or "\\" in value:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{label} must be a repository-relative POSIX path: {value!r}")
    parts = value.split("/")
    if any(part in ("", ".", "..") for part in parts):
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{label} contains an empty, '.' or '..' component: {value!r}")
    return PurePosixPath(*parts)


def _canonical_id(task_id: str, *, allow_root: bool) -> str:
    path = _safe_relative(task_id, "task-id")
    value = path.as_posix()
    for root in ROOTS:
        if value == root:
            if allow_root:
                return value
            raise TaskCtlError(f"task-id names a task root, not a task: {value}")
        if value.startswith(root + "/"):
            return value
    raise TaskCtlError(
        f"task-id must be an exact path below .cswd/tasks or docs/changes: {task_id!r}"
    )


def _cli_task_id(value: str, *, allow_root: bool = False) -> str:
    if value in ROOTS or any(value.startswith(root + "/") for root in ROOTS):
        return _canonical_id(value, allow_root=allow_root)
    shorthand = _safe_relative(value, "CLI task")
    return _canonical_id(f".cswd/tasks/{shorthand.as_posix()}", allow_root=allow_root)


def _resolved_inside(repo: Path, relative: str, label: str) -> Path:
    lexical = repo.joinpath(*PurePosixPath(relative).parts)
    try:
        resolved = lexical.resolve()
    except (OSError, RuntimeError) as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"cannot resolve {label} {relative!r}: {exc}") from exc
    if not _is_relative_to(resolved, repo):
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{label} escapes repository through a symlink: {relative}")
    return lexical


def _task_dir(repo: Path, task_id: str, *, allow_root: bool) -> Path:
    root = _normalize_repo(repo)
    canonical = _canonical_id(task_id, allow_root=allow_root)
    return _resolved_inside(root, canonical, "task-id")


def task_dir(repo: Path, task_id: str) -> Path:
    """Return the safe absolute directory for an exact canonical task ID."""
    return _task_dir(repo, task_id, allow_root=False)


def _validate_source(source: Any) -> str:
    if not isinstance(source, str):
        raise TaskCtlError("source must be a string")
    path = _safe_relative(source, "source")
    if path.name != "spec.md":
        raise TaskCtlError("source must end in spec.md")
    return path.as_posix()


def _validate_blocked_by(value: Any) -> list[dict[str, str]]:
    if not isinstance(value, list):
        raise TaskCtlError("blocked-by must be a YAML list")
    result: list[dict[str, str]] = []
    seen: set[str] = set()
    for index, item in enumerate(value):
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            raise TaskCtlError(f"blocked-by[{index}] must be a mapping")
        unknown = set(item) - {"task-id", "remarks"}
        if unknown:
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"blocked-by[{index}] has unknown key(s): {', '.join(sorted(map(str, unknown)))}"
            )
        if "task-id" not in item:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"blocked-by[{index}] is missing task-id")
        dependency = _canonical_id(item["task-id"], allow_root=False) if isinstance(item["task-id"], str) else None
        if dependency is None:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"blocked-by[{index}].task-id must be a string")
        if dependency in seen:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"blocked-by contains duplicate task-id: {dependency}")
        seen.add(dependency)
        record = {"task-id": dependency}
        if "remarks" in item:
            if not isinstance(item["remarks"], str):
                raise TaskCtlError(f"blocked-by[{index}].remarks must be a string")
            record["remarks"] = item["remarks"]
        result.append(record)
    return result


def _validate_config(value: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:
    if not isinstance(value, dict):
        raise TaskCtlError("task control must be a YAML mapping")
    unknown = set(value) - CONFIG_KEY_SET
    if unknown:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"unknown task control key(s): {', '.join(sorted(map(str, unknown)))}")
    candidate = dict(value)
    missing = [key for key in ("type", "status") if key not in candidate]
    if missing:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"task control is missing required key(s): {', '.join(missing)}")
    if not isinstance(candidate["type"], str) or candidate["type"] not in TYPES:
        raise TaskCtlError("type must be impl or hld")
    if not isinstance(candidate["status"], str) or candidate["status"] not in STATUSES:
        raise TaskCtlError(
            "status must be new, critic, planned, ready, verified, or done"
        )
    if "order" in candidate:
        order = candidate["order"]
        if isinstance(order, bool) or not isinstance(order, int) or order < 0:
            raise TaskCtlError("order must be a nonnegative integer (not bool)")
    if "priority" in candidate:
        priority = candidate["priority"]
        if not isinstance(priority, str) or priority not in PRIORITIES:
            raise TaskCtlError("priority must be P0, P1, P2, or P3")
    if "blocked-by" in candidate:
        candidate["blocked-by"] = _validate_blocked_by(candidate["blocked-by"])
    if "source" in candidate:
        candidate["source"] = _validate_source(candidate["source"])
    return {key: candidate[key] for key in CONFIG_KEYS if key in candidate}


def parse_config(text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Parse and validate one YAML control blob, including content read from Git."""
    return _validate_config(_load_yaml(text, "task control"))


def _validate_repo_config_paths(repo: Path, config: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:
    for blocker in config.get("blocked-by", []):
        directory = task_dir(repo, blocker["task-id"])
        _resolved_inside(repo, directory.relative_to(repo).as_posix(), "dependency task-id")
    source = config.get("source")
    if source is not None:
        _resolved_inside(repo, source, "source")


def _read_text(path: Path, label: str) -> str:
    try:
        return path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except (OSError, UnicodeError) as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"cannot read {label} {path}: {exc}") from exc


def get_task(repo: Path, task_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Read and validate one exact canonical task control."""
    root = _normalize_repo(repo)
    canonical = _canonical_id(task_id, allow_root=False)
    directory = task_dir(root, canonical)
    control = directory / "task.yml"
    _resolved_inside(root, control.relative_to(root).as_posix(), "task control")
    if not control.is_file():
        raise TaskCtlError(f"task control not found: {control}")
    config = parse_config(_read_text(control, "task control"))
    _validate_repo_config_paths(root, config)
    return config


def _yaml_text(value: Any) -> str:
    return yaml.safe_dump(value, sort_keys=False, default_flow_style=False, allow_unicode=True)


def _atomic_write(path: Path, text: str, *, mode: int | None = None) -> None:
    temporary: str | None = None
    try:
        path.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(
            mode="w",
            encoding="utf-8",
            dir=path.parent,
            prefix=f".{path.name}.",
            delete=False,
        ) as stream:
            temporary = stream.name
            stream.write(text)
            stream.flush()
            os.fsync(stream.fileno())
        if mode is None:
            mode = (path.stat().st_mode & 0o777) if path.exists() else 0o644
        os.chmod(temporary, mode)
        os.replace(temporary, path)
        temporary = None
    except OSError as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"cannot atomically write {path}: {exc}") from exc
    finally:
        if temporary is not None:
            try:
                os.unlink(temporary)
            except OSError:
                pass


def set_task(repo: Path, task_id: str, updates: dict[str, Any], replace: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Merge or replace a task control, validating completely before mutation."""
    root = _normalize_repo(repo)
    canonical = _canonical_id(task_id, allow_root=False)
    if not isinstance(updates, dict):
        raise TaskCtlError("updates must be a mapping")
    if not isinstance(replace, bool):
        raise TaskCtlError("replace must be bool")
    unknown = set(updates) - CONFIG_KEY_SET
    if unknown:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"unknown task control key(s): {', '.join(sorted(map(str, unknown)))}")

    directory = task_dir(root, canonical)
    control = directory / "task.yml"
    if directory.exists() and not directory.is_dir():
        raise TaskCtlError(f"task path is not a directory: {directory}")
    _resolved_inside(root, control.relative_to(root).as_posix(), "task control")
    existed = control.is_file()
    if not existed:
        candidate: dict[str, Any] = {"type": "hld", "status": "new"}
    elif replace:
        candidate = {}
    else:
        candidate = get_task(root, canonical)
    candidate.update(updates)
    config = _validate_config(candidate)
    _validate_repo_config_paths(root, config)
    if existed and not replace and not updates:
        return config

    created_directory = False
    if not directory.exists():
        parent = directory.parent
        _resolved_inside(root, parent.relative_to(root).as_posix(), "task parent")
        if not parent.is_dir():
            raise TaskCtlError(f"task parent directory does not exist: {parent}")
        try:
            directory.mkdir()
            created_directory = True
        except OSError as exc:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"cannot create task directory {directory}: {exc}") from exc
    try:
        _atomic_write(control, _yaml_text(config))
    except TaskCtlError:
        if created_directory:
            try:
                directory.rmdir()
            except OSError:
                pass
        raise
    return config


def _canonical_from_directory(repo: Path, directory: Path) -> str:
    try:
        relative = directory.relative_to(repo).as_posix()
    except ValueError as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"task directory is outside repository: {directory}") from exc
    return _canonical_id(relative, allow_root=False)


def _direct_records(repo: Path, canonical: str, *, diagnostics: bool = False) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    directory = _task_dir(repo, canonical, allow_root=True)
    if not directory.is_dir():
        raise TaskCtlError(f"task list container not found: {directory}")
    records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    try:
        children = sorted(directory.iterdir())
    except OSError as exc:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"cannot enumerate task controls below {directory}: {exc}") from exc
    for child in children:
        if not child.is_dir() and not child.is_symlink():
            continue
        control = child / "task.yml"
        spec = child / "spec.md"
        has_control = control.exists() or control.is_symlink()
        has_spec = spec.exists() or spec.is_symlink()
        if not has_control and not has_spec:
            continue
        task_id = _canonical_from_directory(repo, child)
        try:
            _resolved_inside(repo, child.relative_to(repo).as_posix(), "child task directory")
            if not child.is_dir():
                raise TaskCtlError(f"child task path is not a directory: {child}")
            _resolved_inside(repo, control.relative_to(repo).as_posix(), "task control")
            if has_spec:
                _resolved_inside(repo, spec.relative_to(repo).as_posix(), "task specification")
            if not control.is_file():
                raise TaskCtlError(f"direct child task control not found: {control}")
            config = get_task(repo, task_id)
            records.append({"task-id": task_id, **config})
        except TaskCtlError as exc:
            if not diagnostics:
                raise
            records.append({"task-id": task_id, "error": str(exc)})
    records.sort(
        key=lambda record: (
            1 if "order" not in record else 0,
            record.get("order", 0),
            record["task-id"],
        )
    )
    return records


def scan_tasks(repo: Path, task_id: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """Report each direct child's valid control or error without hiding siblings."""
    root = _normalize_repo(repo)
    canonical = _canonical_id(task_id, allow_root=True)
    return _direct_records(root, canonical, diagnostics=True)


def detect_cycle(edges: Mapping[str, Iterable[str]]) -> None:
    """Raise TaskCtlError with a deterministic cycle path when a graph cycles."""
    if not isinstance(edges, Mapping):
        raise TaskCtlError("dependency graph must be a mapping")
    normalized: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
    for node, dependencies in edges.items():
        if not isinstance(node, str):
            raise TaskCtlError("dependency graph node names must be strings")
        if isinstance(dependencies, (str, bytes)) or not isinstance(dependencies, Iterable):
            raise TaskCtlError(f"dependencies for {node!r} must be an iterable of strings")
        values = list(dependencies)
        if not all(isinstance(value, str) for value in values):
            raise TaskCtlError(f"dependencies for {node!r} must be strings")
        normalized[node] = values

    visiting: set[str] = set()
    visited: set[str] = set()

    def visit(node: str, stack: list[str]) -> None:
        if node in visiting:
            start = stack.index(node)
            raise TaskCtlError("dependency cycle: " + " -> ".join(stack[start:] + [node]))
        if node in visited:
            return
        visiting.add(node)
        stack.append(node)
        for dependency in normalized.get(node, []):
            visit(dependency, stack)
        stack.pop()
        visiting.remove(node)
        visited.add(node)

    for node in sorted(normalized):
        visit(node, [])


def _dependency_configs(
    repo: Path,
    initial: Iterable[dict[str, Any]],
) -> tuple[dict[str, dict[str, Any]], set[str]]:
    configs = {record["task-id"]: {key: value for key, value in record.items() if key != "task-id"} for record in initial}
    missing: set[str] = set()
    pending = list(configs)
    while pending:
        task_id = pending.pop()
        if configs[task_id]["status"] == "done":
            continue
        for blocker in configs[task_id].get("blocked-by", []):
            dependency = blocker["task-id"]
            if dependency in configs or dependency in missing:
                continue
            control = task_dir(repo, dependency) / "task.yml"
            if not control.is_file():
                missing.add(dependency)
                continue
            configs[dependency] = get_task(repo, dependency)
            pending.append(dependency)
    edges = {
        task_id: [
            blocker["task-id"]
            for blocker in config.get("blocked-by", [])
            if blocker["task-id"] in configs
        ]
        if config["status"] != "done"
        else []
        for task_id, config in configs.items()
    }
    detect_cycle(edges)
    return configs, missing


def _has_descendant_control(repo: Path, task_id: str) -> bool:
    return bool(_direct_records(repo, task_id))


def list_tasks(repo: Path, task_id: str, impl: bool = False) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """List direct-child controls, optionally filtering runnable impl leaves."""
    root = _normalize_repo(repo)
    canonical = _canonical_id(task_id, allow_root=True)
    records = _direct_records(root, canonical)
    configs, missing = _dependency_configs(root, records)
    if not impl:
        return records
    result: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    for record in records:
        current = record["task-id"]
        if record["type"] != "impl" or record["status"] == "done":
            continue
        if _has_descendant_control(root, current):
            continue
        dependencies = [item["task-id"] for item in record.get("blocked-by", [])]
        if any(dependency in missing for dependency in dependencies):
            continue
        if not all(configs[dependency]["status"] == "done" for dependency in dependencies):
            continue
        result.append(record)
    return result


def _validate_plan_blockers(value: Any, index: int) -> list[dict[str, str]]:
    if value is None:
        return []
    if not isinstance(value, list):
        raise TaskCtlError(f"plan candidate[{index}].blocked-by must be a list")
    result: list[dict[str, str]] = []
    seen: set[str] = set()
    for blocker_index, item in enumerate(value):
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"plan candidate[{index}].blocked-by[{blocker_index}] must be a mapping"
            )
        unknown = set(item) - {"task-id", "remarks"}
        if unknown:
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"plan candidate[{index}].blocked-by[{blocker_index}] has unknown key(s): "
                + ", ".join(sorted(map(str, unknown)))
            )
        token = item.get("task-id")
        if not isinstance(token, str) or not token:
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"plan candidate[{index}].blocked-by[{blocker_index}].task-id must be a nonempty string"
            )
        if token in seen:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"plan candidate[{index}] has duplicate blocker: {token}")
        seen.add(token)
        record = {"task-id": token}
        if "remarks" in item:
            if not isinstance(item["remarks"], str):
                raise TaskCtlError(
                    f"plan candidate[{index}].blocked-by[{blocker_index}].remarks must be a string"
                )
            record["remarks"] = item["remarks"]
        result.append(record)
    return result


def plan_tasks(repo: Path, parent_id: str, candidates: Any) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """Return a deterministic, collision-annotated direct-child plan without writes."""
    root = _normalize_repo(repo)
    parent = _canonical_id(parent_id, allow_root=False)
    parent_directory = task_dir(root, parent)
    spec = parent_directory / "spec.md"
    _resolved_inside(root, spec.relative_to(root).as_posix(), "parent specification")
    if not spec.is_file():
        raise TaskCtlError(f"parent specification not found: {spec}")
    if not isinstance(candidates, list):
        raise TaskCtlError("plan input must be a YAML list")

    normalized: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    slugs: set[str] = set()
    for index, item in enumerate(candidates):
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            raise TaskCtlError(f"plan candidate[{index}] must be a mapping")
        unknown = set(item) - {"slug", "type", "priority", "blocked-by"}
        if unknown:
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"plan candidate[{index}] has unknown key(s): {', '.join(sorted(map(str, unknown)))}"
            )
        missing = [key for key in ("slug", "type", "priority") if key not in item]
        if missing:
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"plan candidate[{index}] is missing key(s): {', '.join(missing)}"
            )
        slug = item["slug"]
        if not isinstance(slug, str) or not SLUG_RE.fullmatch(slug):
            raise TaskCtlError(
                f"plan candidate[{index}].slug must be unique lowercase kebab-case starting with a letter"
            )
        if slug in slugs:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"duplicate plan candidate slug: {slug}")
        slugs.add(slug)
        task_type = item["type"]
        if not isinstance(task_type, str) or task_type not in TYPES:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"plan candidate[{index}].type must be impl or hld")
        priority = item["priority"]
        if not isinstance(priority, str) or priority not in PRIORITIES:
            raise TaskCtlError(f"plan candidate[{index}].priority must be P0, P1, P2, or P3")
        normalized.append(
            {
                "slug": slug,
                "type": task_type,
                "priority": priority,
                "blocked-by": _validate_plan_blockers(item.get("blocked-by"), index),
                "input-index": index,
            }
        )

    internal_edges: dict[str, list[str]] = {candidate["slug"]: [] for candidate in normalized}
    for candidate in normalized:
        for blocker in candidate["blocked-by"]:
            token = blocker["task-id"]
            if token in slugs:
                internal_edges[candidate["slug"]].append(token)
            else:
                _canonical_id(token, allow_root=False)
                task_dir(root, token)
    detect_cycle(internal_edges)

    by_slug = {candidate["slug"]: candidate for candidate in normalized}
    remaining = set(by_slug)
    emitted: list[str] = []
    emitted_set: set[str] = set()
    while remaining:
        ready = [
            by_slug[slug]
            for slug in remaining
            if all(dependency in emitted_set for dependency in internal_edges[slug])
        ]
        if not ready:
            raise TaskCtlError("dependency cycle in plan candidates")
        chosen = min(ready, key=lambda value: (int(value["priority"][1]), value["input-index"]))
        emitted.append(chosen["slug"])
        emitted_set.add(chosen["slug"])
        remaining.remove(chosen["slug"])

    width = max(2, len(str(len(emitted))))
    ids = {
        slug: f"{parent}/{order:0{width}d}-{slug}"
        for order, slug in enumerate(emitted, start=1)
    }
    source = f"{parent}/spec.md"
    proposals: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    for order, slug in enumerate(emitted, start=1):
        candidate = by_slug[slug]
        blockers: list[dict[str, str]] = []
        seen: set[str] = set()
        for blocker in candidate["blocked-by"]:
            dependency = ids.get(blocker["task-id"], blocker["task-id"])
            if dependency in seen:
                raise TaskCtlError(f"plan candidate {slug!r} resolves duplicate blocker: {dependency}")
            seen.add(dependency)
            converted = {"task-id": dependency}
            if "remarks" in blocker:
                converted["remarks"] = blocker["remarks"]
            blockers.append(converted)
        config = _validate_config(
            {
                "type": candidate["type"],
                "status": "new",
                "order": order,
                "priority": candidate["priority"],
                "blocked-by": blockers,
                "source": source,
            }
        )
        destination = task_dir(root, ids[slug])
        collision = destination.exists() or destination.is_symlink()
        proposals.append({"task-id": ids[slug], **config, "collision": collision})
    return proposals


def _parse_order(value: str) -> Any:
    parsed = _load_yaml(value, "--order value")
    return parsed


def _single_option(values: list[Any] | None, name: str) -> Any:
    if not values:
        return None
    if len(values) != 1:
        raise TaskCtlError(f"{name} may be supplied only once")
    return values[0]


def _set_updates(args: argparse.Namespace) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], bool]:
    scalar_values = {
        "type": _single_option(args.types, "--type"),
        "status": _single_option(args.statuses, "--status"),
        "order": _single_option(args.orders, "--order"),
        "priority": _single_option(args.priorities, "--priority"),
        "source": _single_option(args.sources, "--source"),
    }
    field_used = any(value is not None for value in scalar_values.values()) or args.blocked is not None
    whole_count = int(args.yaml is not None) + int(args.all_yaml is not None)
    if whole_count > 1:
        raise TaskCtlError("positional YAML and --all are mutually exclusive")
    if whole_count and field_used:
        raise TaskCtlError("whole YAML replacement and field options are mutually exclusive")
    if whole_count:
        text = args.yaml if args.yaml is not None else args.all_yaml
        value = _load_yaml(text, "whole task control")
        if not isinstance(value, dict):
            raise TaskCtlError("whole task control must be a YAML mapping")
        return value, True
    if not field_used:
        return {}, False
    updates = {key: value for key, value in scalar_values.items() if value is not None}
    if "order" in updates:
        updates["order"] = _parse_order(updates["order"])
    if args.blocked is not None:
        blockers: list[Any] = []
        for text in args.blocked:
            value = _load_yaml(text, "--blocked value")
            if isinstance(value, dict):
                blockers.append(value)
            elif isinstance(value, list):
                blockers.extend(value)
            else:
                raise TaskCtlError("each --blocked value must be a mapping or list of mappings")
        updates["blocked-by"] = blockers
    return updates, False


def _print_yaml(value: Any) -> None:
    sys.stdout.write(_yaml_text(value))


def _build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description=__doc__,
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    parser.add_argument("--repo", default=".", help="repository/worktree root (default: cwd)")
    commands = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)

    get_parser = commands.add_parser("get", help="read one control value or sibling spec path")
    get_parser.add_argument("task")
    get_selectors = get_parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    get_selectors.add_argument("--all", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="all")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--type", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="type")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--status", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="status")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--order", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="order")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--priority", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="priority")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--blocked", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="blocked-by")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--source", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="source")
    get_selectors.add_argument("--spec", dest="selector", action="store_const", const="spec")

    set_parser = commands.add_parser("set", help="merge fields or replace a complete control")
    set_parser.add_argument("task")
    set_parser.add_argument("yaml", nargs="?", help="whole replacement YAML mapping")
    set_parser.add_argument("--all", dest="all_yaml", help="whole replacement YAML mapping")
    set_parser.add_argument("--type", dest="types", action="append")
    set_parser.add_argument("--status", dest="statuses", action="append")
    set_parser.add_argument("--order", dest="orders", action="append")
    set_parser.add_argument("--priority", dest="priorities", action="append")
    set_parser.add_argument("--source", dest="sources", action="append")
    set_parser.add_argument(
        "--blocked",
        action="append",
        help="YAML blocker mapping/list; repeat, or pass [] to clear",
    )

    list_parser = commands.add_parser("list", help="list direct-child controls")
    list_parser.add_argument("task")
    list_parser.add_argument("--impl", action="store_true", help="only dependency-ready unfinished impl leaves")
    list_parser.add_argument("--full", action="store_true", help="emit complete records instead of task IDs")

    plan_parser = commands.add_parser("plan", help="propose deterministic numbered direct children")
    plan_parser.add_argument("parent")
    plan_parser.add_argument("yaml", help="YAML list of slug/type/priority/blocker candidates")

    return parser


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    parser = _build_parser()
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    repo = Path(args.repo)
    try:
        if args.command == "get":
            canonical = _cli_task_id(args.task)
            if args.selector == "spec":
                directory = task_dir(repo, canonical)
                spec = directory / "spec.md"
                root = _normalize_repo(repo)
                _resolved_inside(root, spec.relative_to(root).as_posix(), "task specification")
                print(spec.resolve())
                return 0
            config = get_task(repo, canonical)
            if args.selector in (None, "all"):
                _print_yaml(config)
            elif args.selector == "blocked-by":
                _print_yaml(config.get("blocked-by", []))
            else:
                value = config.get(args.selector)
                print("" if value is None else value)
            return 0
        if args.command == "set":
            canonical = _cli_task_id(args.task)
            updates, replace = _set_updates(args)
            _print_yaml(set_task(repo, canonical, updates, replace=replace))
            return 0
        if args.command == "list":
            canonical = _cli_task_id(args.task, allow_root=True)
            records = list_tasks(repo, canonical, impl=args.impl)
            if args.full:
                _print_yaml(records)
            elif records:
                sys.stdout.write("".join(record["task-id"] + "\n" for record in records))
            return 0
        if args.command == "plan":
            canonical = _cli_task_id(args.parent)
            candidates = _load_yaml(args.yaml, "plan input")
            _print_yaml(plan_tasks(repo, canonical, candidates))
            return 0
        raise TaskCtlError(f"unsupported command: {args.command}")
    except TaskCtlError as exc:
        print(f"task_ctl: error: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
